<title>SOUTH KOREA: BOK steps in foward forex trading - dealers.</title>
<headline>BOK steps in foward forex trading - dealers.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The central Bank of Korea (BOK) sold some $20 million in the one-month forward trading during Tuesday afternoon trading to slow the won's fall against the dollar, dealers said.  </p>
<p>The intervention took place as the domestic unit fell to around the 874.00 mark against the dollar, they said.</p>
<p>They said this was the first time the BOK has intervened in forward trading. But the central bank denied stepping into the market, as it usually does.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5644</p>
</text>
